MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Bread, Frankie Valli, and the Eagles feel like natural next choices because I have repeatedly chosen older hits and best-of collections, especially melodic songs and classic rock.",
    "Glen Campbell connects with the easygoing folk side of my listening, while That's Christmas To Me fits my latest seasonal choice. Partners also connects with the vocal duet appeal of Cheek to Cheek."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Adele albums feel less relevant right now because my repeated interest is in older hit collections; having listened to Born This Way does not mean contemporary pop is my main interest.",
    "Tornado gives me too little indication of familiar songs or a connection to my listening to choose it over the clearly relevant hits collections."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The contemporary pop choices seem to give too much importance to one part of my history compared with my repeated selections of older music.",
    "A connection to vocal albums is only part of the appeal: Partners interests me, but that connection alone does not make it as compelling as an older hits collection."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated choices of best-of albums and nostalgic compilations suggest that familiar songs matter alongside the artist or musical style.",
    "My latest Christmas purchase makes seasonal music relevant now, while my older listening still helps distinguish which nonseasonal collections I would choose first."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations mostly capture my interest in melodic older hits, but some give too much weight to my occasional contemporary pop listening."
}
